%description:

RFC 768 — a sender that generates a checksum transmits a nonzero value, and a sender that
generates none transmits zero; the receiver accepts a datagram of either kind.

Checks RFC768-CKSUM-2 (description). Also covers RFC768-CKSUM-1 (description, presence only)
from doc/project/evidence/standard/rfc768/catalog.md. The English procedure and the mockup are
in doc/project/evidence/protocol/udp/checks.md#checksum-presence-and-absence; the program steps
below map one to one onto its expected observations. Mapping of the mockup: host A = hostA,
host B = hostB, host C = hostC; link 1 = hostA-hostB, link 2 = hostB-hostC.

Udp's checksum mode is the `checksumMode` parameter of the ~Udp module
(src/inet/transportlayer/udp/Udp.ned), `@enum("disabled", "declared", "computed")`, default
"declared". Only two of the three values are usable here: "computed" makes the sender compute
and transmit the real RFC 768 checksum (a nonzero value, or all-ones if the sum came out zero);
"disabled" makes it transmit an all-zero checksum, i.e. RFC768-CKSUM-2's "generated none". The
third value, "declared", is a non-serializable simulation shortcut (a placeholder value of
0xC00D, asserted correct without being computed) and is not one of the two RFC 768 behaviours,
so it is not used by either host here. Host A therefore sets `*.hostA.udp.checksumMode =
"computed"`, host C sets `*.hostC.udp.checksumMode = "disabled"`.

Implementation note verified in Udp.cc: when checksumMode is "computed", Udp::initialize()
(INITSTAGE_TRANSPORT_LAYER) dynamically creates a UdpChecksumInsertionHook submodule and
registers it as an IPv4 datagramPostRoutingHook; the header's checksum field is left as 0x0000
at packet-creation time and is only filled in by that hook during IP post-routing -- still
strictly before the packet reaches the link layer, so it is already final wherever this program
observes it (link 1). The "disabled" (and "declared"/"declared-incorrect") modes instead set
the checksum field synchronously in Udp::insertChecksum() at packet-creation time; no hook is
involved.

Deviation on observations 2 and 4 ("hands ... upward"): as established in
tests/protocol/ipv4/Rfc791DatagramDelivery.test and reused in Rfc768DatagramDelivery.test,
UdpSink's own "packetReceived" signal cannot be observed by the tester; the proxy is
Udp::sendUp()'s packetSentToUpperSignal, and because the UDP header is already stripped by
then, host A's and host C's datagrams are told apart at host B by size (100 vs 200 octets),
exactly as checks.md's own Notes prescribe.

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("rfc768_checksum")
        // Expected observation 1: link 1 shows host A's datagram to port 5000 with a nonzero
        // checksum -- confirms the stimulus of the first half (a checksum was generated).
        .once(on("hostA.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .packet("udp.destPort == 5000 && udp.totalLengthField == 108B && udp.checksum != 0")
                  .describe("host A's 100-octet datagram on link 1 with a nonzero checksum")
                  .within(0.5))
        // Expected observation 2: host B's UDP hands the 100 octets upward -- the datagram
        // with a checksum was accepted.
        .once(on("hostB.udp").signal("packetSentToUpper")
                  .match([](const MatchContext& c) {
                      return c.event.packet->getByteLength() == 100;
                  })
                  .describe("host A's 100 octets handed up from host B's UDP, accepted with a checksum")
                  .within(0.1))
        // Expected observation 3: link 2 shows host C's datagram to port 5000 with an
        // all-zero checksum -- confirms the stimulus of the second half (no checksum was
        // generated).
        .once(on("hostC.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .packet("udp.destPort == 5000 && udp.totalLengthField == 208B && udp.checksum == 0")
                  .describe("host C's 200-octet datagram on link 2 with an all-zero checksum")
                  .within(0.2))
        // Expected observation 4: host B's UDP hands the 200 octets upward -- the datagram
        // without a checksum was accepted, not discarded as a failed one.
        .once(on("hostB.udp").signal("packetSentToUpper")
                  .match([](const MatchContext& c) {
                      return c.event.packet->getByteLength() == 200;
                  })
                  .describe("host C's 200 octets handed up from host B's UDP, accepted without a checksum")
                  .within(0.1));
}

%activity:
// present only so opp_test compiles the %global above; this module is not in the network.
EV << "rfc768_checksum compiled\n";

%file: test.ned

import inet.node.ethernet.Eth100M;
import inet.node.inet.StandardHost;
import inet.networklayer.configurator.ipv4.Ipv4NetworkConfigurator;

// The mockup of doc/project/evidence/protocol/udp/checks.md#checksum-presence-and-absence:
// hostA -- hostB -- hostC, host B between the other two, no forwarding needed (both sends
// terminate at host B itself).
network Rfc768ChecksumNet
{
    submodules:
        configurator: Ipv4NetworkConfigurator { @display("p=100,50"); }
        hostA: StandardHost { @display("p=200,100"); }
        hostB: StandardHost { @display("p=400,100"); }
        hostC: StandardHost { @display("p=600,100"); }
    connections:
        hostA.ethg++ <--> Eth100M <--> hostB.ethg++; // link 1 (hostB.eth[0])
        hostB.ethg++ <--> Eth100M <--> hostC.ethg++; // link 2 (hostB.eth[1])
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
network = Rfc768ChecksumNet
sim-time-limit = 1s
seed-set = 0

# Static ARP keeps the wire free of ARP request/reply noise.
**.ipv4.arp.typename = "GlobalArp"

# Host A generates a real checksum; host C generates none (transmits an all-zero checksum).
*.hostA.udp.checksumMode = "computed"
*.hostC.udp.checksumMode = "disabled"

# Host A: 100 octets to port 5000.
*.hostA.numApps = 1
*.hostA.app[0].typename = "UdpBasicApp"
*.hostA.app[0].destAddresses = "hostB"
*.hostA.app[0].destPort = 5000
*.hostA.app[0].localPort = 4000
*.hostA.app[0].messageLength = 100B
*.hostA.app[0].startTime = 0.1s
*.hostA.app[0].sendInterval = 1s

# Host C: 200 octets to port 5000, starts 0.1s after host A.
*.hostC.numApps = 1
*.hostC.app[0].typename = "UdpBasicApp"
*.hostC.app[0].destAddresses = "hostB"
*.hostC.app[0].destPort = 5000
*.hostC.app[0].localPort = 4001
*.hostC.app[0].messageLength = 200B
*.hostC.app[0].startTime = 0.2s
*.hostC.app[0].sendInterval = 1s

# Host B: one receiving program, on port 5000.
*.hostB.numApps = 1
*.hostB.app[0].typename = "UdpSink"
*.hostB.app[0].localPort = 5000

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST rfc768_checksum: PASS
